\par\par \b \uc2  U.S.-Japan  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  action not seen enough to cap yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 1999\par 13:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 3 (Reuters) - The risk the United States could join Japan in attempting to curb industry-crippling yen strength spooked \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers into selling yen on Tuesday but analysts doubted such an action would have a lasting impact. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa conjured up the spectre of coordinated U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by mentioning he had discussed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements with U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers in a telephone conversation on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The mere thought of what might have been discussed persuaded dealers to sell yen where blunter threats of solo Japanese action had failed. The comment lifted the dollar/yen exchange rate 1.5 percent away from Monday's 5-1/2-month lows. However, analysts questioned whether the yen would see more than a temporary setback even if the U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly for the first time in about a year. \par \par \uc2  "The risk of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen following Miyazawa's comments, which revealed some discomfort in Japan about the strength of the yen," said Avinash Persaud, head of global research at State Street in London. \par \par \uc2  "We would get a short spike in dollar/yen to 118 if we got it, but this would merely represent a good opportunity to go long yen again." \par \par \uc2  He put the chances of the U.S. authorities selling yen on their own account, rather than on behalf of Japan as they did on on July 20, at about 30 percent in the wake of Miyazawa's comments from 10 percent previously. \par \par \uc2  Dollar gains to 118 yen after any joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would leave it 2-1/2 yen higher than it is currently trading and make the action more successful than any of the Bank of Japan's recent solo attempts to engineer a weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  Japan's efforts to prevent yen strength from derailing its economic recovery have seen its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on at least seven occasions since June 10, with at least two rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted in July. \par \par \uc2  However, the dollar is about five percent weaker against the yen than it was when the Bank of Japan first mounted its campaign to curb demand for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I am surprised they have left it so long and let dollar/yen fall so far, but they may just be putting together a bear trap," said Lee Ferridge, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Rabobank in London. \par \par \uc2  Analysts doubted whether a one-off display of unity by the U.S. and Japanese authorities would dampen demand for yen any more effectively. \par \par \uc2  "The success of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot be judged on how much it pushes up the spot rates but by whether it changes perception about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy or whether it is a 24-hour wonder," said Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Paribas Capital Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  "While repeated rounds of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may change the perception, the impact of just one round would be limited." \par \par \uc2  Persaud at State Street expects joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would fail to undermine the yen sustainably given the size of capital repatriation that could be seen ahead of the end of the Japanese fiscal half year in September. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be swamped by these sorts of flows so we are looking for dollar/yen to fall to around 105 by September, whether we get joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or not." \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv83036v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
