\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar battered vs yen with BOJ absent from market. \b0\par\par\uc2 639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 1999\par 09:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 2 (Reuters) - The dollar was battered further \par \par \uc2  against the yen by late afternoon on Monday, slumping to a new \par \par \uc2  5-   month low of 114.13 yen as selling accelerated when \par \par \uc2  authorities showed no signs of stepping into the market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's weakness also reflected market jitters about U.S. asset markets amid signs the U.S. economy is overheating. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's decline accelerated on selling by institutional investors and speculators disappointed with the greenback's earlier inability to break decisively above 115 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 114.35/45 yen at 0633 GMT, compared with 114.47/57 yen in late New York trade on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The 115 yen point was psychologically important and the failure to push the dollar above it weighed on the market," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Monday he was watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market carefully. \par \par \uc2  Separately, senior Finance Ministry official Haruhiko Kuroda said a premature rise in the yen was not good for the Japanese, Asian or global economies. \par \par \uc2  "We are ready to act when necessary in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Kuroda said. But dealers said market speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had faded as there had been no action to back up the words since July 21. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets a number of times since June 10 to curb a resurgence in the yen against the dollar, sparked mainly by data showing a jump in growth in the Japanese economy in the January-March quarter. \par \par \uc2  Yutaka Kawazoe, a manager at the Industrial Bank of Japan's International Treasury Department, said: "Even if they (the BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it would be unlikely to prop up the dollar for long as the market is struggling to reduce long positions in the dollar." \par \par \uc2  He also said the BOJ is unlikely to step in as Tokyo stocks fell only fractionally on Monday, in contrast with Wall Street's sharp fall on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, a former senior Japanese policy-maker said in a newspaper article on Monday that Japan should drop its decades-old aversion to a strong yen. \par \par \uc2  Toyoo Gyohten, a former special adviser to Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi, said in a commentary in business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun that Japan's "strong-yen phobia" had influenced policy in recent years far more than warranted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real effect on the economy. \par \par \uc2  "Japan's economy has been seized by fear of a strong yen for nearly 30 years, and we should break that spell," said Gyohten, now director of the Institute for International Monetary Affairs. \par \par \uc2  The vicious circle set off by a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can happen in any country, "but no other nation shows stronger rejection symptoms than Japan", he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said substantial stop-loss dollar selling orders were expected first at 114 yen, followed by 113.80 yen. Those levels are also trigger points for knock-out options. \par \par \uc2  But they cited profit-taking and sporadic buying by Japanese importers as supporting the dollar's downside, as the market was still wary of possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's external reserves rose to a record $260.694 billion at the end of July, up $14.317 billion from a month earlier. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, dealers and investors will be keeping an eye on two key economic reports in the U.S. - a survey of the nation's manufacturing sector to be released on Monday, and the monthly employment report due on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo stock market's benchmark Nikkei 225 average closed down 36.16 points or 0.20 percent at 17,825.70 on Monday. ((Mariko Hayashibara, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 1396 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv820373g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
