   OTHR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1998------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par AVG DEC   35.0  2.3   4.4  7.7  5.3 14.6\tab 23.7    1.2    5.8\par AVG NOV   35.1  2.2   4.2  8.0  5.5 14.4\tab 24.4    0.9    5.2\par AVG OCT   35.8  2.3   3.9  9.6  6.6 10.9\tab 23.4    0.1    6.9\par AVG SEP   35.9  2.5   4.3  8.5  6.3 15.0\tab 22.4    0.9    4.2\par AVG AUG   37.1  2.8   4.6  8.3  6.7 16.0\tab 19.2    1.0    4.5\par AVG JUL   39.0  2.9   4.6  8.0  6.0 15.1\tab 19.5    1.1    3.8\par AVG JAN   37.1  2.6   6.0  9.5  5.0 14.3\tab 21.0    1.6    2.9\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab      -- Reuters New York-based asset allocation survey\par \tab \tab      -- Reuters Tokyo-based asset allocation survey\par \tab \tab      -- Reuters Britain-based asset allocation survey\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Andrew Priest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     LONDON, July 30 (Reuters) - European global fund managers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are shifting assets into Japanese bonds, betting on further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains for the resurgent yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A monthly Reuters poll of continental Europe based global\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fund managers released on Friday showed average allocations to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese bonds rose to 7.9 percent of global fixed income\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par portfolios from 6.4 percent in June's poll.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fund managers cited the prospects of further yen strength\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the strongly underweight position most funds held previously\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as the main drivers of the push to own more Japanese bonds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We moved up our Japanese weighting hoping to profit from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen move," said Jean-Francois Tilquin head of fixed income\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment at Expertise Asset Management in Paris.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The idea was not to be exposed for too long in terms of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par duration but to profit from the strength of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said. "Although we don't want to play too much against the Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Japan."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The yen rose to under 115 yen against an ailing U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Thursday, its strongest level for more than five months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has benefited from renewed confidence\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in its economy and from the fact that the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remained on the sidelines, eschewing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par previously kept the yen close to a 118-120 trading range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tilquin said the 115 yen level was likely to be strongly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par defended by Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , adding there was a strong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par temptation to take some profits at current levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Other fund managers agreed with this cautious line.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Japanese bonds are vulnerable to a build up of debt by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government and either an economic upturn or a desperate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par monetisation of issues as politicians despair of a rebound in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the economy," said Guy Monson, chief investment officer at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sarasin Investment Management.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen could overshoot to up to 105 to the dollar if\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreigners continue to increase weightings to Japanese shares\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and domestic investors stop diversifying overseas deterred by a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rising yen, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Then you have a situation where you have all buyers and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par just one seller, the Bank of Japan, which will be overwhelmed,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the Reuters poll allocations to Japanese equities were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shaved back in July to 11.1 percent of average global equity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par funds from 11.3 percent in June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A weak yen has been a major bonus for recovering Japanese\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par companies, boosting their competitiveness abroad at a time when\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their domestic markets remain sluggish.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As the yen has risen so shares in Japanese exporters have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suffered, with a number of large corporates citing 115 yen as a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par key level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, fund managers increased their holdings of U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par assets and bought more euro zone bonds. Respondents returned\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their portfolio revisions before the stronger-than-expected U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par second quarter employment data was announced on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Even if we get just get one more (U.S.) rate rise I think\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par you're still in a lose-lose situation with U.S. shares," said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monson. "Either earnings fall off because the economy slows or\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the financial markets come down because (Fed Chairman Alan)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Greenspan hits them," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The poll of 11 fund managers based in continental Europe was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par conducted between July 26 and July 29. The global fixed income\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par portfolios are benchmarked against the Salomon Brothers global\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bond index while the equity portfolios are benchmarked against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Morgan Stanley Capital International World Index.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((London Capital Markets +44 171 542 5113 fax +44 171 583\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 7239 email:andrew.priest@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7u03hjr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
