\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar falls to lowest in over five months vs yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1999\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 29 (Reuters) - The dollar fell to its lowest in more than five months against the yen on Thursday, undermined by broad-based weakness in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the absence of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign exchanges so far. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen fell as low as 115.25 by 0952 GMT according to Reuters data, down from an overnight peak of 116.10 and its weakest since February 15. Its losses gathered momentum after stop-loss orders to sell dollars were triggered by the break below 115.35 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have been encouraged to buy yen in the past week as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the strength of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  even after it broke free on July 22 of the ranges which had contained it against the dollar since mid-February. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan's recent absence was in marked contrast to the strategy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly it had pursued since June 10. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least seven times between June 10 and July 21, including once through the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and once through the U.S. Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  The absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the yen to benefit on Thursday from a report showing Japanese industrial output rose by a larger-than-expected 3.0 percent in June and a 1.65 percent increase in Japan's Nikkei stock average overnight. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro was at 123.20/40 yen, near session lows and weaker than 123.48/67 late in Europe on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Swaha Pattanaik, London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7t03nlt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
