\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr edges down, wariness on BOJ provides cushion. \b0\par\par\uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1999\par 06:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 29 (Reuters) - The dollar edged below 116 yen by Tokyo midday on Thursday, as an uptrend in JGB yields and Nikkei share prices reflecting robust Japan June industrial output data induced fresh yen buying, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar gradually drifted down to a session low of 115.45 yen, but the market was cautious about selling it too aggressively from that level amid wariness of possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. \par \par \uc2  At 0315 GMT, the dollar stood at 115.55/65 yen compared with 116.08/18 yen in late New York on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The yen strengthened, especially after JGB yields started rising sharply, but the market was somewhat cautious about bidding the yen up too aggressively from current levels," a Japanese trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market saw strong support at Wednesday's Tokyo low of 115.38 yen and short-covering interest by U.S. fund operators slightly below 115.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  Persisting rumours that an Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would buy dollars to protect its knockout options orders lined up at 115 yen also made operators cautious about selling the greenback too aggressively on dips, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Trade Ministry said industrial output in June rose by 3.0 percent from the previous month. The average forecast of economists polled by Reuters was a 1.7 percent rise. \par \par \uc2  The Trade Ministry forecast that industrial output would rise 0.5 percent month-on-month in July and by 3.7 percent in August. \par \par \uc2  At 0331 GMT, the yield of the August 214th 10-year JGB had risen by 10 basis points to 1.80 percent. \par \par \uc2  The key Nikkei 225 share index was up 204.04 or 1.16 percent at 17,783,95. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/yen will seek for direction from the Nikkei and from JGBs. The market is very keen about reacting to yen-buying incentives amid current sentiment," a city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "But the dollar's fall to near 115 yen should increase fear of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  Although the market reacted little to senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi's remarks on Thursday, dealers were cautious about going overly short on dollars because of the possibility of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi said Japanese authorities were always carefully watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and thinking of appropriate measures. \par \par \uc2  But Mizoguchi, head of the ministry's International Bureau, declined to comment on rumours that Japanese authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday, or on specific \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels or on the pace of movements. \par \par \uc2  Asked if he thought the recent pace of the dollar's fall against the yen was excessive, Mizoguchi said: "I will not comment on specific levels or the pace." \par \par \uc2  Rumours about the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had spread in the market on Wednesday after the dollar rapidly jumped from a low of 115.38 yen to above 116 yen. Dealers later said the rebound may have been caused by options-linked bids from U.S. hedge funds. \par \par \uc2  The euro moved in tight ranges as the market refrained from taking new positions ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's council meeting later in the day, although many operators were not expecting change in its credit policy, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0403 GMT, the euro stood at $1.0658/61 against $1.0655/62 in late New York on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A wait-and-see mood also spread by late morning ahead of key U.S. gross domestic product (GDP) and Employment Cost Index (ECI) data scheduled for release later on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Economist polled by Reuters estimated, on average, that GDP grew by 3.3 percent in the second quarter. They said the U.S. Labor Department's ECI probably rose 0.8 percent in the second quarter after a very subdued 0.4 percent in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  ((Chikafumi Hodo, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7t03mx7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
