\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr/yen falls below 115 yen to lowest since Feb 15. \b0\par\par\uc2 276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1999\par 15:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, July 29 (Reuters) - The dollar fell against the Japanese yen to hit its lowest level in more than five months amid unexpectedly weak growth numbers from the United States that followed surprisingly strong data from Japan. \par \par \uc2  Just as U.S. trading got underway, the dollar fell below the psychologically significant 115-yen level to a low of 114.92, a level not seen since February 15, according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen started New York trading at 115.25/35, already down from Wednesday's 116.08/18 close, and then fell further as dealers reacted to news that the U.S. economy grew at a 2.3-percent rate in the second quarter, well down from the 4.3-percent rate of the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  "There's general bearishness to the dollar after the market reacted nervously to the numbers and the weakness of the dollar came out most in the yen, because there were stops triggered around 115," said Jeffrey Yu, senior dealer at Sanwa Bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had slipped to fresh lows overnight after Japan posted a better-than-expected jump in industrial output growth. According to Japan's trade ministry, June output rose by three percent from May, its biggest rise in 2-1/2 years. \par \par \uc2  Dealers remain on the lookout for possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially after the bank has been conspicuously absent in the past week and a senior Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said overnight Japanese authorities are carefully watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  ((Elizabeth Lazarowitz, NA Treasury Desk, 212-859-1607)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7t03fv3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
