\par\par \b \uc2  MOF Mizoguchi/No Comment -2: After Dlr Jumps About Y1 \b0\par\par\uc2 136 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 1999\par 09:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Zembei Mizoguchi, the head of the international bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Wednesday afternoon that he wouldn't comment on whether or not the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  He told a small group of reporters that he would also not comment on specific dollar/yen levels. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi said Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy remains unchanged. \par \par \uc2  "All I can say is that our stance is unchanged," he said. \par \par \uc2  Rumors of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared soon after the dollar quickly jumped about Y1 higher around 0657 GMT Wednesday. The dollar had been trading around Y115.40, its lowest since February. At 0737 GMT the dollar is trading around Y115.58. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 28-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0739GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7s05npk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
