\par\par \b \uc2  Rift/BOJ/MOF/Report -2: BOJ Worried About Money Mkt Ops \b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 1999\par 03:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by tapping money from a special \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund, which is funded by having the BOJ underwrite FBs. The FBs in the pool are rolled over automatically, said a source at the ministry, according to the report. \par \par \uc2  Therefore, until \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  reverses course and begins conducting yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - adding yen to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund, the BOJ will be stuck with its holdings of FBs. FBs are short-term government securities issued to cover temporary shortages in government funds. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ fears that large holdings of FBs will make money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  less effective by reducing the variety of assets held at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It's also afraid that the Finance Ministry might use the fact that the BOJ is already underwriting FBs as an excuse to prod it to underwrite long-term government bonds - a step that the BOJ has vehemently opposed, the paper reported. \par \par \uc2  Japan is the only major industrialized nation where fiscal authorities can unilaterally force the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to finance \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the paper quoted a Japanese analyst as saying. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 28-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0121GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7s05mnl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\p