\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED-TOCOM PGMs close down by limit. \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 1999\par 10:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Corrects name of exchange in fourth paragraph) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 28 (Reuters) - Yen-based platinum group metal (PGM) futures ended at daily limit lows on Wednesday, as palladium was hit by news that Russia intended to stabilise supply of palladium in the world market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The yen's rise against the dollar sent all precious metals contracts tumbling, they said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, Norilsk Nickel, the world's largest palladium producer, said it had agreed with Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to coordinate policy on selling the metal in a move analysts say should make prices less volatile. \par \par \uc2  On New York's NYMEX, PGMs slid after the report. \par \par \uc2  "(Tokyo) palladium fell in sympathy with the drop in New York overnight, but later it was also dragged by a strong yen and platinum, which was sold actively by trading houses on weak technicals," said a commodities brokerage analyst. \par \par \uc2  All palladium futures ended by their limit low of 40 yen, with benchmark June closing at 1,187 yen. \par \par \uc2  Selling gained momentum as the benchmark contract breached 1,200 yen in the afternoon, traders said. \par \par \uc2  All platinum contracts closed by their limit low of 50 yen, with benchmark June ending at 1,206 yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders said gold futures simply reacted to the strength of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while spot prices were largely unchanged from the previous day. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, gold marked a record low for the benchmark for the fourth consecutive day, reflecting persistent bearish sentiment, they said. \par \par \uc2  Gold futures ranged from flat to 12 yen per gram lower. Benchmark June ended off 10 yen at a new low of 926 yen. \par \par \uc2  Silver ended mostly lower, ranging from 1.1 yen per 10 grams higher to 2.7 yen lower. Benchmark June ended 2.7 yen lower at 184.6 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar sank to a fresh five-month low against the yen in hectic late Tokyo trading only to rebound on rumours the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 7431 tokyo.commodit.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7s03g6s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
