\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar erases gains vs yen amid absence of BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 1999\par 09:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 26 (Reuters) - The dollar erased earlier gains against the yen by late trade on Monday as the market grew impatient with its stiff upside amid absence of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar earlier rose as high as 117.09 yen mainly on short-covering, but speculative sales from overseas operators and interbank players, as well as apparent offers from Japanese exporters pushed the dollar back down, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 116.47/57 yen at 0635 GMT against 116.52/62 yen in late New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  By 0653 GMT, the dollar went as deep as 116.45 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "(Many market players) built longs in morning trade, but started taking profits after waiting in vain for the dollar to go higher," a city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said rumours of bids from public funds and trust banks sitting around 116.50 yen were supporting the dollar for the time being. \par \par \uc2  Defence of an option-strike point believed to be near 116 yen was also supporting the dollar's downside. \par \par \uc2  The dollar went as low as 116.05 yen last Thursday in New York. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at another city bank said: "In the absence of BOJ dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far today, the market is probing the dollar's downside. I think this will be intensified, especially when overseas markets open." \par \par \uc2  He added: "I don't think the BOJ will step in until the dollar slides below 116 yen." \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi reiterated on Monday that a rapid, premature rise in the yen was not appropriate, and that the ministry would take action if needed. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi declined to comment on the outlook for the dollar/yen rate. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also remained weak against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as jitters about U.S. inflation kept the greenback's tone bearish, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Inflation fears were sparked after U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan warned last Thursday that the Fed would raise interest rates at the first sign of higher inflation. \par \par \uc2  Given this warning, the market remained wary ahead of key economic data to be released on Thursday, including U.S. second-quarter growth and employment cost index data. \par \par \uc2  The pound was quoted at $1.5833/43, compared with $1.5770/80 in late New York on Friday, helped by upbeat reports on the British economy in weekend press reports, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was also firmer versus the dollar, quoted at $1.0524/29, compared with $1.0508/15 in late New York. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami, addressing a meeting of BOJ branch managers, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep its current easy monetary policy until concern over deflation disappeared. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa later said he supported the BOJ policy, but the market reacted little to his remarks. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers kept an eye on expectations of Japanese growth. MITI said on Monday that overall business activity in May rose 1.8 percent from the previous month, and that the tertiary sector index also rose in May, 1.4 percent month-on-month. ((Mariko Hayashibara, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 Tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7q03wnu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
