\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Watch:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Tones Down Use Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  In Shift \b0\par\par\uc2  By Takeshi Takeuchi \par \uc2 823 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1999\par 12:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Though the rhetoric regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels remains the same, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shifted its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in the last few weeks and abandoned previous attempts to keep the dollar above Y120. \par \par \uc2  The new approach follows criticism of the active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy by Lawrence Summers, the new U.S. Treasury Secretary, and the departure of Eisuke Sakakibara from Japan's Finance Ministry. \par \par \uc2  His successor as vice Finance Minister for International Affairs, Haruhiko Kuroda, has used \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb excess volatility, rather than defending a line in the sand at Y120. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan and the Finance Ministry have given up manipulating the market to push up the dollar against the yen through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," said Yukihiko Hashimoto, assistant manager and strategist of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Sanwa Bank. "The BOJ now only aims at smoothing dollar/yen moves." \par \par \uc2  In an interview with CNBC television earlier this month, Summers criticized the old strategy of aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying: "I think the focus in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to be on strengthening the fundamentals, which goes back to domestic demand led-growth...not seeking to manipulate \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Without the prospect of U.S. support, Japan would have found it increasingly difficult to stave off the market's appetite for yen. \par \par \uc2  The overt U.S. criticism coincided with the the departure of the flamboyant Sakakibara, who had tended to favor an aggressive approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Though the Finance Ministry insists that policy remains unchanged, analysts say the style is bound to change. \par \par \uc2  "Mr. Sakakibara was a very political person," said Sanwa's Hashimoto. "His style of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was somewhat coercive, and political needs at a given time were the main factor affecting his decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  "Now that he has retired from the post, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  approach has been normalized," he added. \par \par \uc2  Some BOJ Officials Had Doubts About \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  There was also some longstanding resistance to the aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  approach within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to some sources close to the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  "Some officials had doubts about the wisdom of artificially pushing the dollar above Y120 in the face of market forces," one of the sources said. \par \par \uc2  "It was common sense among international monetary officials that a country can't control its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels for long through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone," he added, speaking on condition of anonymity. \par \par \uc2  The July 5 release of the BOJ's "tankan" business survey also raised doubts about aggressive attempts to manipulate the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, sources said. Among other things, the survey showed that Japanese corporations believe they can remain profitable even with the dollar as low as Y116-Y117. \par \par \uc2  Japan would therefore open itself to charges of tyring to export its way out of recession if it tried to keep the yen from strengthing beyond Y120. "Some BOJ officials appeared to be worried about that possibility," said another source, also speaking on condition of anonymity. \par \par \uc2  All of which explains why Japan has sharply reduced its dollar-buying in recent weeks. In a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that began in June and culminated with the July 5 release of the tankan, Japan sold yen to the tune of about $20 billion. As a result, the dollar rose as high as Y122.87 on that day. \par \par \uc2  Market Sentiment Turns Dollar-Bearish \par \par \uc2  But with market sentiment increasingly bullish about Japan's economic prospects, the dollar has since come under attack again. This time, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't tried too hard to stop the move, buying only about $2 billion of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this week. Furthermore, the BOJ refrained from stepping into the market Thursday despite the yen's rise to a five-month high of Y116.05. \par \par \uc2  Friday the dollar was quoted around Y116.50 late in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The return to the orthodox approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't likely to be an easy adjustment for the BOJ, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Lingering anxiety over the possibility of another interest rate hike in the U.S. and concerns about the health of U.S. stock prices have turned many traders into dollar-bears, they noted. \par \par \uc2  "Overseas investors are beginning to prepare for a shift out of dollar-denominated assets to assets in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - including the yen," said Shuji Takano, assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at ABN AMRO Bank. \par \par \uc2  Under such circumstance, any dollar buying by the BOJ would easily be absorbed by yen hungry investors, diminishing the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. As a result, the dollar could move toward a test of support at Y110 in the near term, some said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Now that the BOJ has gone back to smoothing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy, it must carefully choose the timing of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to ensure yen levels consistent with the aim of an economic recovery,"\par said Takano.\par  By Takeshi Takeuchi; 813-5255-2934; ttakeuchi@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-07-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1021GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1042 4131 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7n05j1n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
