\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr/Yen Up, But Heavy On Offers From US Funds \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hidenobu Kageyama \par \uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1999\par 07:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar rebounded from its overnight plunge in Tokyo Friday, ending the session about a half-yen higher than levels in New York Thursday, but traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upside remains heavy amid steady selling interest from U.S. hedge funds. \par \par \uc2  The dollar began Friday's session just under Y117.00 - up from an intraday low of Y116.05 Thursday - and drifted higher on buying by Japanese importers and banks making purchases on behalf of pension funds. The dollar rose as high as Y117.45 before selling from U.S. hedge funds put an end to the recovery. \par \par \uc2  "Bids from Japanese players supported the dollar Friday in Asia while offers from U.S. hedge funds were seen waiting at Y117.50-60," said Yukohiko Hashimoto, vice president at Sanwa Bank. \par \par \uc2  Traders were nervous throughout the session about the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but all has been quiet at the Bank of Japan Friday. \par \par \uc2  That said, several top officials reiterated warnings about an overly strong yen, with Economic Planning Agency chief Taichi Sakaiya warning that "sudden yen strength" wouldn't be good and noted that the current dollar/yen rate isn't necessarily acceptable. \par \par \uc2  Zembei Mizoguchi, head of the Finance Ministry's international bureau, said a rapid strengthening of the yen is inappropriate at this early stage of the economic recovery. The remark had little impact on trading, however. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y117.10, above Y116.60 late Thursday in New York but down from Y117.38 late Thursday in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0490, lower than $1.0517 late Thursday in New York and below $1.0528 in London Thursday. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y123.00, up from Y122.63 in New York late Thursday but below Y123.58 in London late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5825, slightly up from $1.5815 in New York late Thursday. Sterling was at $1.5787 in London late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 23-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0529GMT \par \par \uc2  1034 1863 28038 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7n05ig5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
