\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo:Dlr Up On Fears Of Possible BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1999\par 02:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar is higher in early Tokyo trading Friday from its late Thursday levels in New York, on short covering by market participants amid fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  "Overseas funds and Japanese players are buying dollars for yen this morning to cover short positions after the sharp fall of the dollar overnight and on expectations that the BOJ might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  today," a dealer at a Japanese trust bank said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar plunged as low as Y116.05 in New York late Thursday on renewed concerns of U.S. inflation, which were sparked by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's Humprhey-Hawkins testimony to the House Banking Committee. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan told the committee that the Federal Reserve Bank remains worried that inflation could reemerge if the U.S.'s unemployment rate continues to fall. He said the Fed will act "promptly and forcefully" to counteract any inflationary pressures. \par \par \uc2  Although the BOJ did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in New York late Thursday, dealers believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Tokyo Friday. The dollar is still under downward pressure, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be very effective since many market players are either short or have neutral positions, they said. \par \par \uc2  A further drop in the Nikkei stock average, following the fall of the Dow Jones In $1.0525 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 23-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0015GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7n05hxw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
