\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dollar trembles above 116 yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1999\par 12:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 23 (Reuters) - The dollar teetered above the previous day's five-month lows against the yen by the European midsession on Friday, with dealers poised to push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to new depths. \par \par \uc2  Lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  fuelled yen gains after U.S. assets and the dollar were bruised by a hawkish testimony from U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan's absence has encouraged the yen bulls to probe forward," said Robert Hayward, senior economic adviser at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 116.38/48 yen at 1003 GMT, one yen below its overnight high but above Thursday's low of 116.00. \par \par \uc2  The 116 yen level was the dollar's weakest since February 16 and four percent below Monday's high against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar followed U.S. bonds and stocks down after Greenspan said the Fed would act "promptly and forcefully" if it saw evidence of a pick-up in inflation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were becoming more daring after the BOJ failed to prevent the yen strengthening beyond 117.50 per dollar, the level at which Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started a series of at least seven yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 10. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese authorities made it very clear they wanted to keep dollar/yen in a 118-122 band to try and stop a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  adversely affecting what modest economic recovery is taking place in Japan," said Andrew Milligan, director of economic research at Morely Fund Management in London. \par \par \uc2  "They've lost that battle overnight because we broke through some important resistance levels. Unless they do something we look poised to go towards 112." \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said overnight that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  all the time was not always the best way to tackle yen strength. \par \par \uc2  This week's yen gains have come despite two bouts of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ, on Tuesday and Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro also fell against the yen, to a low of 122.18/31 by 1020 GMT, from 123.42/47 late in Europe on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But the euro held the $1.05 level against the dollar, after rising to a two-month high of $1.0574 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The euro has risen by as much as four percent against the dollar this week, from Monday's low of $1.0120. \par \par \uc2  "Thus far, the price action has been driven by interbank, proprietary traders and leveraged accounts," said Nick Parsons, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Paribas, in a client note. \par \par \uc2  "The big, big move we are looking for, to $1.10 plus, will require corporate flows as well," he added. \par \par \uc2  The euro was little moved by German inflation and euro zone industrial production data released on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The key German states of Hesse, Baden-Wuerttemberg and Bavaria issued higher than expected consumer price index data for July. Hesse's CPI rose 0.5 percent month-on-month, while inflation in the other states rose 0.4 percent from June. \par \par \uc2  Euro zone industrial production adjusted for working days fell 0.8 percent in May compared with May, 1998. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Eugenio Domingo Solans said Spain needed to pay special attention to inflation. \par \par \uc2  Governments needed to respond to inflation diffrences in the euro zone by meeting the terms of the stability pact and boosting competition in markets, he added. \par \par \uc2  ECB chief economist Otmar Issing said euro zone economic growth of two percent was not unrealistic this year. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7n03ua9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
