\par\par \b \uc2  MOF Mizoguchi -2: After Quick Rise In Dollar/Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 134 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 09:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Zenbei Mizoguchi, international bureau chief at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Wednesday he would not comment on whether or not the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  But he repeated the ministry is carefully watching the moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to reporters at the ministry, Mizoguchi said, "(We) are always watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market situation carefully. We always take appropriate steps." \par \par \uc2  Regarding a market rumor that the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on Wednesday, Mizoguchi said, "I cannot comment on whether or not the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  today." \par \par \uc2  The dollar quickly rose about half a yen around 0710 GMT Wednesday. At 0734 GMT, the dollar was at Y119.12 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0735GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7l05gn0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
