\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Seen Facing Tougher Fight As Dlr Weakens Across Bd \b0\par\par\uc2  By Marianne Sullivan \par \uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 16:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The Bank of Japan's battle to slow the yen's appreciation is getting even tougher as the dollar begins weakening across the board. \par \par \uc2  Since June 10, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has conducted a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stall what it deemed the yen's premature appreciation. Until last week it was working in line with a trend: The bank was pushing for the dollar to move higher against the yen at the same time as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was hitting multi-year highs against the euro and Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  "Now the BOJ has to fight against a strong tide," said Henry Willmore, senior economist at Barclays Capital in New York. \par \par \uc2  Until this week, the BOJ was fighting this battle only on one front. It was attempting to prevent the yen from appreciating before a more evident recovery in the Japanese economy. In essence, it was working in the direction of both Japanese and U.S. fundamentals. The appreciation the BOJ was fighting was the product of foreign-investment flows into Japan's Nikkei 225 stock index, which has soared some 30% this year. \par \par \uc2  But now, the dollar is moving lower against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , namely the euro and Swiss franc, and its downward pressure against the yen also increases. \par \par \uc2  "That means it will be more difficult for the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to be effective. To increase the effectiveness, the BOJ is either going to have to increase the size of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or change its tactics," said Robert Lynch, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Paribas in New York. \par \par \uc2  By the opening of trading in New York, the dollar had already sunk below Y118.60 despite a fresh round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, which drove it as high as Y119.69. \par \par \uc2  Even what one trader called the "classic bear trap" impressively laid by the BOJ Tuesday - which caught a sizable number of yen-enthusiasts off guard - failed to generate sufficient momentum to create a more lasting effect. \par \par \uc2  -By Marianne Sullivan; 201-938-4385 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-07-99 \par \par \uc2  1414GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7l05etp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
