\par\par \b \uc2  MOF Mizoguchi/ \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: After Dollar Falls Below Y120 \b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 02:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Zembei Mizoguchi, head of the international bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Wednesday that the ministry will take appropriate steps against an excessive strengthening of the yen if needed. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to a small group of reporters upon entering the ministry, Mizoguchi said, "We will take proper action against an overly strong yen if needed." \par \par \uc2  He also said that he is "watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets carefully. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the finance ministry wants to keep the dollar above Y120.00, Mizoguchi only said, "I have no comment," adding "As a general rule, I don't comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels." \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi's remarks come in the wake of the yen's sharp rise earlier this week and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in New York late Tuesday to stem this rise. \par \par \uc2  At 0022 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y119.20, and the euro was trading at Y124.16. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0023GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7l05ej3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
