\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dollar sizes up lows vs yen, euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 12:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 21 (Reuters) - The dollar traded close to its lows against the yen and the euro by the European midsession, despite earlier dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Top Japanese financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda confirmed the BOJ sold yen for dollars on Wednesday, which traders saw in late Tokyo trade from levels around 118.70 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was proving less successful, after at least seven moves to curb yen strength since June 10. \par \par \uc2  "The more often it occurs, the less significant is the impact of such an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Klaus Kusber, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 119.04/09 at 1001 GMT, after rising from a low of 118.63 to a high of 119.66 on the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably succeed in holding dollar/yen above the 117.50 level that has acted as a floor since March. Further dollar gains were unlikely while investors were bullish about the Japan's economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  "Money will continue to flow into yen assets until we have figures showing the Japanese economy is still in trouble," said Fabio Fraschetti, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banca Nazionale del Lavoro. \par \par \uc2  The euro held onto most of its gains against the yen, boosted by the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's progress against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen was trading at 124.42/57 at 1014 GMT, from a high of 124.92 and from 123.78/87 in late European trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro climbed to its highest level against the dollar since June 25, consolidating gains made on Tuesday after Germany's closely watched Ifo business climate index rose to a nine-month high in June. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at $1.0464/69, from highs of $1.0475 and from $1.0399/06 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A fall in the euro to below parity with the dollar, widely predicted only days ago, was looking less likely, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The Ifo index, a record U.S. trade deficit in May and concerns about U.S. stocks were all working in the euro's favour, they added. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very short of European assets," said Fraschetti. "This will favour a portfolio adjustment towards Europe, and put the euro in a $1.05-$1.10 range." \par \par \uc2  The euro was also buoyant against other European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hitting its highest since June against Norwegian and Swedish crowns and peaks since May against the pound. \par \par \uc2  The pound recovered slightly from 10-week lows against the euro and rose by as much as half a cent against the dollar after minutes of the July meeting of the Bank of England's Monetary Policy Committee showed a unanimous vote in favour of steady rates. \par \par \uc2  The unanimous vote fuelled a perception in the market that UK rates have bottomed out at 5.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  UK retail sales were unchanged in May from the previous month, but rose 3.8 percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  Euro/sterling was trading at 66.44/50 pence at 1033 GMT, from a high of 66.65 and from 66.27/32 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling/dollar was at $1.5728/38 from a high of $1.5756 and from $1.5686/96 late in Europe on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The MPC said the exchange rate had eased slightly since its June meeting, when it cut rates by 25 basis points. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at 102.6 against its trade-weighted index, compared with a high of 104.7 when the MPC started its June meeting on June 9. \par \par \uc2  ((Carolyn Cohn, London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7l03zu7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
