\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE-Dollar/yen jumpy as euro/dlr climbs. \b0\par\par\uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1999\par 10:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 21 (Reuters) - The dollar jumped from its lows below 119 yen at the European open on Wednesday, as Tokyo traders cited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro, meanwhile, rose to its highest against the dollar in July, supported by an improving growth outlook for the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ can hold dollar/yen around 119, it will cost them a lot of money but they have plenty of yen to sell," said Adrian Schmidt, international economist at Chase. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo traders said the Bank of Japan was seen to have bought dollars for yen from around 118.70 in late Tokyo trade. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 119.10/20 yen at 0744 GMT, from a low of 118.63 and after a high of 119.66 after the BOJ was sighted, and from 118.98/03 in late European trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Zembei Mizoguchi declined to comment on the rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Top Japanese financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda confirmed overnight that the Bank of Japan sold yen for dollars via the U.S. Federal Reserve on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least six times since June 10 to curb the yen's strength, holding the dollar above 117.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said there were too many natural buyers of yen, amid signs of an economic recovery in Japan, to push the dollar much higher. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan may be providing support, but dollar/yen looks vulnerable and seems like it will retest the downside," said Martin Squires, head of research at Rudolf Wolff & Co. \par \par \uc2  "Each time they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  the dollar is lifted but then struggles to hold its gains," he added. \par \par \uc2  Concerns about the U.S. stock market were weighing on the dollar against the euro after the Dow Jones Industrial Average closed down 1.71 percent on Tuesday, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at $1.0454/57 at 0804 GMT, its highest level since June 25 and a rise of 3.5 percent from life lows of $.10104 set on July 13. \par \par \uc2  "There is concern about the stock market in the U.S., while there is more confidence in the European recovery," said Schmidt. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there was little new impetus for the euro on Wednesday, but Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to benefit from Tuesday's news of a rise in Germany's closely-monitored Ifo business climate index to a nine-month high in June. \par \par \uc2  Scandinavian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell against the euro on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro hit its highest level since June 2 of 8.2615 Norwegian crowns, while euro/Swedish crown rose to 8.7855, its highest since June 17. \par \par \uc2  "The euro is playing catch-up against the Scandis," said a dealer from a UK bank. "The euro is the ship to be on, at least for the moment, and no one wants to be caught short." \par \par \uc2  The euro rose to 10-week highs against the pound before the release of minutes of the July meeting of the Bank of England's Monetary Policy Committee meeting, due at 0830 GMT. \par \par \uc2  UK June retail sales data are also due at 0830 GMT, and are forecast to rise by 0.2 percent from May. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at highs of 66.50/55 pence at 0816 GMT, from 66.27/32 late in Europe on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the pound was at $1.5711/14 from $1.5686/96 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Carolyn Cohn, London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7l03zu4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
