\par\par \b \uc2  Fed/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -3: Estimated At $500 Million \b0\par\par\uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1999\par 16:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  U.S. traders said the Fed is continuing to buy dollars for yen to keep the dollar above about Y119.20. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. trader estimated that the Federal Reserve bought $500 million in dollars for yen Tuesday on behalf of the Bank of Japan. "Not very much," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  The trader said the Fed appeared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on three separate occasions. First, it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the largely transparent Electronic Brokering Systems (EBS), then it made a direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through a bank counterparty, which it then followed with another round on EBS, he said. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  both confirmed Tuesday the Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on their behalf. \par \par \uc2  "It's true that we entrusted the New York Fed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said an official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's New York office. "We arranged for the Fed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on our behalf," said an official at the Bank of Japan's representative office in New York. \par \par \uc2  U.S. analysts noted, however, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  produced little more than a one-yen rise in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  John McCarthy, senior vice president, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at ING Barings Capital Markets in New York, said that fundamentals - especially the growing U.S. trade deficit with Japan - are in favor of a stronger yen, and for that reason the Fed wouldn't buy dollars for yen on its own account. \par \par \uc2  "My guess is the market is long and will look for opportunities to sell. So I don't see a big rally in the dollar/yen even if they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again," McCarthy said. \par \par \uc2  Data Tuesday showed the U.S. trade gap widened to a record $21.34 billion in May, from $18.59 billion in April, exceeding expectations. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also has found pressure against the yen as fund managers buy Japanese stocks on signs the Japanese economy is starting to recover. The benchmark Nikkei-225 stock index has gained more than 30% so far this year. \par \par \uc2  Japanese markets were closed Tuesday for a holiday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Treasury and Federal Reserve have declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The market's reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "isn't overwhelming. We haven't been able to get close to Y120.00," said Bob Sinche, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank in New York. \par \par \uc2  "We think there is still the risk that with Japanese bond yields up, with investors in Japan suffering serious losses on euro-denominated bonds - both from a price point-of-view and a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  point-of-view - there is the potential for more of those funds to come back to Japan," Sinche said. "That flow will continue to support the yen." \par \par \uc2  Until the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducts "unsterilized" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , allowing considerably more yen into the banking system and returning to an easier monetary stance, the market's bias will continue to lean toward a stronger yen, Sinche said. \par \par \uc2  At 10 a.m. EDT, the dollar was trading at Y119.34, down from a high of Y119.80 but still up from Y118.30 at Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 20-07-99 \par \par \uc2  1419GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 1863 28038 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7k05cts\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
