\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-Yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -more sizzle than steak? \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 690 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1999\par 21:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, July 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  swooped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday in its latest attempt to stem the yen's strength against the dollar, but analysts questioned the move's lasting power in a market hungry for Japanese assets. \par \par \uc2  Responding to a wave of yen selling orchestrated by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  - its sixth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in as many weeks - the dollar had charged up more than a full yen to peak at 119.68. \par \par \uc2  But within hours, much of the gains had evaporated. \par \par \uc2  "Right now it is too early to tell whether this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will actually keep the yen down," said Mellon Bank trader Grant Wilson as the dollar listed under 119. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials have made no secret that they consider a stronger yen undesirable for their economy as the nation crawls out of recession on back of a surprisingly strong 1.9 percent real growth rate in the first three months of this year. \par \par \uc2  But analysts and dealers say those nascent signs of recovery are precisely what have attracted investors into Japan and helped the benchmark Nikkei 225 stock index race ahead to a string of record closes for 1999. On Monday the index gained 1.5 percent to 18,532.58 points. Tokyo markets were closed on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The United States' red hot economy continues to outpace growth in Europe and Asia, and the dollar has consequently been very strong against Europe's single euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; investors are keen to get into Japan ahead of the curve. \par \par \uc2  "What we are seeing is capital moving back into the Nikkei and that is helping the yen against the dollar and the euro," Mike Malpede, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Refco Group Ltd, said. \par \par \uc2  Technical analysts agreed that charts, too, pointed to more dollar/yen selling in the near term, with many casting an eye toward 117 yen and lower. \par \par \uc2  "Barring any more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to hold this up, I would suspect another move down to the 117 and we might even take that out," Bank of America analyst Ture Johnson said. \par \par \uc2  John Tirone, technical analyst at Chase Securities, also said the charts pointed to further dollar weakness. \par \par \uc2  "Once the dollar has breached 117.60 yen it will trigger a sell signal in Elliott and regular chart terms suggesting an initial test of 116.90," Tirone added. \par \par \uc2  The market had been bracing for a fresh bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the yen surged 1.3 percent in Monday's U.S. session to reach five week highs against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Few traders were shocked when the Federal Reserve bought dollars for yen on behalf of Japan as U.S. trade got underway on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A representative in the Bank of Japan's New York office confirmed the Fed had acted on its behalf; U.S. authorities declined to comment on the action. \par \par \uc2  Several waves of morning dollar buying, beginning at levels just above 118, supported the greenback. \par \par \uc2  "The timing was not totally surprising and I think the move reinforces the fact we will trade between 122 and 117 yen - but let's see how it pans out" said Tim Fox, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered. \par \par \uc2  The new twist in the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was that it marked the first time the action was conducted through U.S. authorities. A month ago, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had sold yen for euros on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf and other \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were conducted during Tokyo trading hours. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during New York trading prompted some traders to review talk of possible tensions between Japan and the United States sparked by Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers' warning that domestic demand must be stimulated. \par \par \uc2  "The reports of friction read like fiction," Barclays Capital senior economist Henry Willmore said, adding that Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  per se does not shed new light on a conflict that may not even exist. "It is inconceivable that the Fed would not honour its obligation to act on behalf of a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  ((-N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1639 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7k0459c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
