\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Dollar up as Fed sells yen for Bank of Japan. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1999\par 17:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, July 20 (Reuters) - The dollar surged against \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen on Tuesday morning as the Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, selling yen on behalf of the Bank of Japan and pushing the greenback up a full yen. \par \par \uc2  A representative for the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "The Fed has been selling yen for dollars on our behalf," the BoJ official said. \par \par \uc2  It was the sixth time in the past two months that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Japanese officials have warned repeatedly that a premature appreciation of the yen could harm the country's nascent economic recovery. A stronger yen would make Japanese products more expensive in other countries. \par \par \uc2  The Federal Reserve Bank of New York declined to comment. But \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said the New York Fed began selling yen when the dollar stood just above 118 yen. They said the Fed followed through with several more yen sales to keep pushing the yen down. Dealers said the Fed had dealt with them directly and was also seen acting over the electronic broking system. \par \par \uc2  The dollar shot to a session high of 119.68 yen after having opened at 118.17 yen. The exchange rate settled to trade near 119.35 yen per dollar late in the morning, then slipped back to just below 119 yen before noon. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also jumped against the yen, rising to 124.14 yen per euro from an opening level near 123.12. \par \par \uc2  "The Fed (was) in buying dollars for yen but they seem to be doing it on behalf of the Bank of Japan," a trader who had dealt with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The yen had risen against the dollar in recent days, making traders increasingly nervous about the prospect for more Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There have been market palpitations that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be in again and these levels made sense. The selling seems to have been large, but orderly as well," said Grant Wilson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Mellon Bank in Pittsburgh. \par \par \uc2  Traders have been unable to estimate how much the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have spent on this round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank has sold yen for both dollars and euros in recent weeks and dealers see little new significance in the fact that the bank asked the New York Fed to act on its behalf today. \par \par \uc2  "They could have asked the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to do it too but it really does not make much of a difference because the other \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is merely acting as the BoJ's agent," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  There had been some speculation about possible friction between the United States and Japan since Lawrence Summers, the newly appointed Treasury Secretary, recently said there is no substitute for boosting a nation's domestic demand. A weaker yen would tend to boost demand for Japanese products in other countries, not in Japan itself. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said Tuesday's move shed little light on that issue. "The Fed is simply honouring an agreement to act on another \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf and why should they not do that?" asked Henry Willmore, senior economist at Barclays Capital. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the last six weeks. Japanese markets were closed on Tuesday for a market holiday. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7k043y4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
