\par\par \b \uc2  BoJ official confirms Fed sold yen on its behalf. \b0\par\par\uc2 222 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1999\par 16:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, July 20 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan confirmed on Tuesday that the Federal Reserve Bank of New York had sold yen on the BoJ's behalf in early U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  "The Fed has been selling yen on behalf of the bank," an official at the BoJ's New York representative office told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The dollar shot up more than a full yen to a high of 119.68 yen, after opening at 118.12/22 in U.S. trade. It then settled back slightly although traders remained on the lookout for fresh waves of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in the yen over the past two months, as Japanese authorities warned that a premature appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could harm the country's nascent economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dipped below the 118 level on Monday to five-week lows as investors tested the Bank of Japan's commitment to temper the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Treasury said it had no comment on Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also declined to comment on rumours that it was involved in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((-N.A. Treasury Desk +1 212 859 1868)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7k043oo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picw