\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ confounds  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  traders by failure to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 685 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1999\par 14:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers are beginning to think Japan has lost its taste for sparring with the foreign exchanges as the yen scrambles to peaks it was at before the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  began \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  just over a month ago. \par \par \uc2  The campaign to prevent yen gains from choking \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recovery has seen the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least five times since June 10 and spend an estimated $30 billion in the process. \par \par \uc2  Traders have withstood the assault in the knowledge economic fundamentals are on their side, and the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the dollar has fallen back below 118 yen in the past 24 hours is prompting some to question whether Japan has given up trying to persuade them to sell its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "This is either a very subtle bear trap or a change in tactics given \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was very aggressive in jawboning and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  but has been practically silent in the past week," said Paul Meggyesi, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank. \par \par \uc2  "They may just have realised they can't beat a fundamentally driven trend - the BOJ has been acting against portfolio flows attracted by the pick-up in Japanese growth and bond yields rather than against speculative flows." \par \par \uc2  Traders said one reason the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market despite a fall of 2.75 percent in dollar/yen on Monday is that the bulk of the slide took place in North American trading hours and Japan's markets were closed for a public holiday on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  However, the BOJ has been known to leave orders for others central banks to execute on its behalf in the past, most recently on June 18 when it bought euros for yen via the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The euro sank on Monday to a life low of 120.91, down more than three percent since June 18. \par \par \uc2  The absence of any such buying on behalf of the Bank of Japan overnight has reinforced the perception among traders that the United States is loathe to become involved in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Such talk has been rife since Friday after a newspaper reported the U.S. refused a Japanese Finance Ministry request to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its behalf. The report came just over a week after U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers urged Japan to focus on economic fundamentals rather than "manipulating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ". \par \par \uc2  "That report is probably quite credible but Japan may end up going to the next G7 (Group of Seven) meeting on their knees to ask for help anyway," said Chris Iggo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital in London. \par \par \uc2  "If they throw in the towel and let dollar/yen go to 110, the Nikkei will collapse and we could see more bank problems so the risk of allowing that to happen is too great. But given they have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  five or six times and dollar/yen is back where it was, they need to come up with something new." \par \par \uc2  Technical analysts such as Stuart Frost at NatWest Global Financial Markets said there was little need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the charts suggested the dollar was not about to suffer a speedy slump that would threaten a break of 110 yen. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to prove fruitless given that Japanese investors are waiting to bail out of long dollar positions they have built up in the past month. \par \par \uc2  While the cards are stacked against the Bank of Japan, analysts said they may be forced to carry on the war of attrition they have started given the economic consequences of allowing the market to buy yen unchecked. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan is not about to give up just yet given the reasons they were \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  still exist and they need to give the economy more time to recover," said Lee Ferridge, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Rabobank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The market is testing them again, but should be careful because they will come back in." \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7k043hz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
