\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE-Dollar struggles near lows,awaits Ifo. \b0\par\par\uc2 650 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1999\par 09:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 20 (Reuters) - The dollar struggled just above multi-week lows against the euro and yen early in European trading on Tuesday, consolidating after a sharp sell-off in Monday's North American session. \par \par \uc2  All eyes will be on Germany's Ifo business climate data for June due out at 0800 GMT, which could cast light on the health of Europe's biggest economy and determine if the euro's renewed attempt to recover from life-long decline could be sustained. \par \par \uc2  "If the Ifo is stronger, there may be potential for some further gains (in the euro)," said Jeffrey Woodruff, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BankBoston in London. \par \par \uc2  "But if it's pretty much as expected, I think people would be excited to be able to sell at these levels," he added, noting the euro's strong downtrend from January highs. "Even if the number is a little bit better than expected, overall Europe is still in trouble and it's just a better level to sell the euro." \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar stood at $1.0295/00 at 0722 GMT, slightly off a near-three-week high of $1.0336 hit in New York on Monday but well above sub-$1.02 levels in Monday's European session. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese bank trader in London said Monday's euro/dollar rally had begun with short-covering in the euro crosses, suggesting it was based on expectations of strong Ifo numbers. \par \par \uc2  "I think a pretty good number is priced in already," he said. "It could prove to be a selling opportunity if the number isn't that good." \par \par \uc2  Economists surveyed by Reuters last week on average predicted that the headline west German business climate index would rise to 91.1 in June from 90.4 in May. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen struggled within a yen above the 117.68 five-week low set late on Monday, with the market puzzled by a lack of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite the yen's steep rise, over which Japanese officials had repeatedly expressed concerns. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen was last at 118.12/17, up from a late Monday low of 117.68 - just short of the 117.59 low set on June 10 and around levels where the BOJ began its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that eventually took the dollar above 122. \par \par \uc2  Traders said a Japanese holiday on Tuesday might have tied the hands of the BOJ and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could come into the market later in the day. \par \par \uc2  "I think the BOJ has its work cut out for them," Woodruff at BankBoston said. "If they're sticking by what they've been saying - that a premature yen strength is bad for their economy - they're going to have to do something about this." \par \par \uc2  He said the credibility of the Japanese authorities was at stake, adding that the fact that the June 10 low held on Monday could be seen as the market's show of respect for now. \par \par \uc2  "I think the reason the market didn't push it further was that they'd be sort of waving a red flag in front of the BOJ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there were exotic option triggers near 117.50 and huge sell stops below that level, which meant initial retests of the lows could be choppy and slow but the decline would accelerate once support was broken. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, sterling and Swiss franc were firmer against the dollar, aided by the euro's rebound. \par \par \uc2  The pound was at $1.5773/78 against $1.5613/23 late in Monday's European session. Dollar/Swiss was down at 1.5540/50, just above Monday's near-three-week low of $1.5525 but down sharply from 1.5762/72 late in Europe on Monday. ((Shin Kishima, London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7k042iu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
