\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Asia -2: Technical Analysts See Euro Below Y120 \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 1999\par 08:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Technical analysts also agree that the euro is destined to fall further against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  With the market's ceiling at Y123.90 appearing ever more difficult to attain, and support at Y121.70 looking increasingly vulnerable, the majority are looking for a rapid move downward. \par \par \uc2  According to Thio Chin Loo, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banque Paribas, a drop from current levels will trigger stop-loss orders threatening to propel the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  all the way down to test support at Y119.35. \par \par \uc2  And the longer-term outlook is even bleaker. Not only are European institutions still actively buying yen to rebuild their weightings to Japanese investments, according to research issued by Standard Chartered Bank, Asian central banks have begun to cut the proportion of their foreign reserves held in euros, adding to the forces weighing on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  For the time being, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will help to support the euro, but even \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action is unlikely to prove effective should Japanese institutions begin unwinding their European debt investments. \par \par \uc2  "We believe that unwinding is inevitable, and the later that it begins, the more disorderly it will be," wrote State Street analysts in a research note issued on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The period of danger will extend over the summer months, through to the end of the Japanese fiscal half year at the end of September, says State Street, whose analysts warn that: "It is very dangerous to be short yen." \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0609GMT \par \par \uc2  4258 5095 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7j05ayq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
