\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Yen bulls run on, telecoms engage bourses. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jo Winterbottom \par \uc2 782 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 1999\par 13:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 19 (Reuters) - The yen continued to test new \par \par \uc2  highs against the euro and the dollar as the conspicuous absence \par \par \uc2  of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  persuaded traders to test the \par \par \uc2  resolve of authorities to rein in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There's a growing feeling that international support for \par \par \uc2  BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very low, and I think that means we can see \par \par \uc2  a stronger yen," said Francis Breedon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers in London. \par \par \uc2  A quiet start to European stock market trading ahead of some \par \par \uc2  big corporate earnings this week was punctuated by French oil \par \par \uc2  company Elf Aquitaine's $50.8 billion counter-bid for national \par \par \uc2  rival TotalFina and telecoms tie-up talk. \par \par \uc2      The dollar slumped below 120 yen for the first time since \par \par \uc2  June 18, the day the BOJ bought euros for yen, touching 119.97 \par \par \uc2  from 120.88/02 late in Friday's European session while the euro \par \par \uc2  slid to a new life low of 121.67 yen. \par \par \uc2  "It's clear that the (BOJ) threshold is lower now," said a \par \par \uc2  dealer at a Japanese bank in London. "The question is how low." \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda reiterated \par \par \uc2  cooperation between the Group of Seven industrial nations on \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy remained solid but speculation persisted \par \par \uc2  there was displeasure at the U.S. Treasury about micro-managing \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. \par \par \uc2      "The gauntlet's down, we'll see if the Bank of Japan is \par \par \uc2  ready to pick it up this time," said one trader. \par \par \uc2      The euro's weakness against the yen also saw it slipping \par \par \uc2  against the dollar but holding above a record low of $1.0104. \par \par \uc2      Adding to euro woes, Herbert Hax, chairman of Germany's \par \par \uc2  economic advisory council, was quoted by the Welt am Sonntag \par \par \uc2  newspaper as saying the euro could soon fall below parity with \par \par \uc2  the dollar. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Eugenio Domingo Solans \par \par \uc2  was quoted by Spanish newspaper El Mundo saying the bank would \par \par \uc2  not raise rates to help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Euro weakness dragged European government bonds lower and \par \par \uc2  the spread between 10-year U.S. and German bond yields fell \par \par \uc2  below 97 basis points, its lowest since the euro launch in \par \par \uc2  January. \par \par \uc2  European bourses were hesitant ahead of Wall Street's \par \par \uc2  opening, which was expected to be mixed after a record close on \par \par \uc2  Friday at 11,209.84, up 0.21 percent. Big moves are considered \par \par \uc2  unlikely ahead of a bunch of corporate results later this week. \par \par \uc2  Half year results expected this week include SmithKline \par \par \uc2  Beecham and Reuters Group on Tuesday and U.S. giants IBM and \par \par \uc2  Microsoft Corp later on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Shares in TotalFina jumped when they started trading at 1100 \par \par \uc2  GMT after being suspended along with those of Elf, which made a \par \par \uc2  cash and shares counter-bid for the Franco-Belgian energy group \par \par \uc2  at a premium of around 10 percent to Friday's close. \par \par \uc2      TotalFina shares were up 4.76 percent at 136.5 euros while \par \par \uc2  Elf stock gained 1.88 percent to 179.3 euros. \par \par \uc2      Telecommunications were buzzing, with Spain's Telefonica up \par \par \uc2  over one percent after fresh reports it was in merger talks with \par \par \uc2  Deutsche Telekom despite its denial on Friday. Deutsche Telekom \par \par \uc2  eased slightly to 40.30 euros. \par \par \uc2  Britain's biggest cable company Cable and Wireless \par \par \uc2  Communications, edged 0.21 percent lower after it announced it \par \par \uc2  was in exclusive merger talks with Nasdaq-listed rival NTL Inc. \par \par \uc2  And mobile phone company Nokia hit a lifetime high of 97.00 \par \par \uc2  euros on optimism ahead of its announcement of second quarter \par \par \uc2  earnings on Thursday, before later easing back with the Helsinki \par \par \uc2  bourse, which drifted off peaks in thin trade. \par \par \uc2  Gold touched fresh 20-year lows, fixing at $253.15 a troy \par \par \uc2  ounce as increased physical demand and production cutbacks have \par \par \uc2  failed to lift sentiment in a market dominated by Britain's \par \par \uc2  reserve auctions and other sales planned by the International \par \par \uc2  Monetary Fund and Switzerland. \par \par \uc2  Crude prices were slightly lower but still near 20-month \par \par \uc2  highs at $19.43 a barrel struck last week as tough OPEC supply \par \par \uc2  cuts eat into global inventories. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  MARKETS AT 1145 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  (figure in brackets previous London close) \par \par \uc2  $/Euro 1.014 euros (1.0218) $/ Y 119.76 yen (120.94) \par \par \uc2  STOCK MARKETS \par \par \uc2  LONDON - FTSE 100: 6572.6 points, up 9.4 or 0.14 percent \par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT - X-DAX: 5634.46 points, up 14.52 or 0.26 percent \par \par \uc2  PARIS - CAC-40: 4648.33 points, down 8.46 or 0.18 percent \par \par \uc2  PRECIOUS METALS (figures in brackets previous London PM fix) \par \par \uc2   GOLD - $253.9 ($253.15)   SILVER - $5.06 ($5.05) \par \par \uc2   Brent crude oil futures $19.1, down $0.25 \par \par \uc2   ------------------------------------------------------------ \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7j049n3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
