\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Yen remains firm, tests BOJ resolve. \b0\par\par\uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 1999\par 10:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 19 (Reuters) - The yen remained near its highs against the euro and the dollar in Europe on Monday as the market tested the Bank of Japan's resolve to prevent it from rising too much in order to ensure Japan's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The beleagured euro, which fell to new life lows against the yen in Asia near 122.00 yen, was also hovering within a half cent of its $1.0104 all-time low against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "There's a growing feeling that international support for BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very low, and I think that means we can see a stronger yen," said Francis Breedon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers in London. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen was at 122.12/22 yen at 0749 GMT, a touch above its life low and more than a yen below 123.51/68 Friday's late European closing levels. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 120.37/47 yen, barely above a one-month low of 120.30 set earlier and from 120.88/02 late on Friday. Euro/dollar was at $1.0145/50 against Friday's $1.0214/18. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market was nervous about possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but appeared willing to explore how far they could push the dollar and euro down against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "It's clear that the threshold is lower now," said a dealer at a Japanese bank in London. "The question is how low." \par \par \uc2  Breedon at Lehman added that BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was more likely to be in euro/yen than in dollar/yen given the euro's steeper losses and suspected displeasure at the U.S. Treasury about micro-managing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. \par \par \uc2  He added that while any Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be heavy, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authorities might not try to drive the yen down as far as they had did in previous bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It may not be that they would chase it (dollar/yen) all the way up to 122 as they've done before - they may just want to keep it above 120," Breedon said. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese Finance Ministry's new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  czar, Haruhiko Kuroda, said overnight that \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy coordination among the Group of Seven nations remained solid in response to questions about speculated policy differences between Japan and the United States. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Eisuke "Mr. Yen" Sakakibara, whom Kuroda succeeded earlier this month, said Japan needed to curb the yen for three to six months to ensure its economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The euro's renewed slide in Asia was attributed to comment by Herbert Hax, one of Germany's so-called Five Wise Men of economic advisers, who was quoted in Sunday's Welt am Sontag as saying that the euro could soon fall below $1.00. \par \par \uc2  Traders said while Hax's remark was not surprising, it undermined the euro, which was already looking vulnerable after last week's recovery attempt quickly ran out of steam. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Eugenio Domingo Solans was quoted by El Mundo newspaper on Sunday as saying the ECB would not raise interest rates to defend the euro. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, sterling and Swiss franc were soft against the dollar in sympathy with the feeble euro. Sterling/dollar stood at $1.5575/80 against $1.5654/59 late in Friday's Europe and dollar/Swiss was at 1.5830/40 against Friday's 1.5722/32. \par \par \uc2  Euro/sterling was easier at 65.08/12 pence against 65.20/26. ((Shin Kishima, London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, shinichi.kishima@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7j048bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
