\par\par \b \uc2  More misery ahead as euro/yen technicals turn ugly. \b0\par\par\uc2 514 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 1999\par 04:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 19 (Reuters) - The euro's fundamental flaws are compounded by a truly ugly technical picture against the yen that warns of further misery to come. \par \par \uc2  The hapless European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already lost 10 percent of its value against the yen this year and analysts are certain it would have been a lot more if not for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) to curb the yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro squandered a chance for redemption on Monday by fleeing below its former lifetime trough at 122.63 yen to as low as 121.98. In the process the euro ruined a potential double bottom formation that had offered a glimmering of a reversal in the eight month-old downtrend. \par \par \uc2  With that bulwark overrun, analysts had expected support around 122.10/20 to provide only a momentary cushion before a push to the key 121.65/70 level, a trough from August 1997 derived using the old Ecu rate. \par \par \uc2  "We would be strongly bearish below here (121.70)," said an analyst at Standard and Poor's MMS. \par \par \uc2  "Although interaday technicals are moving into oversold territory, the overall bearish bias keeps the focus firmly on selling strategies." \par \par \uc2  By 0200 GMT the euro had slumped to 122.09/26 yen from 123.43 late in New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  A break below 121.65/70 would take the euro to territory not seen since the first half of 1995, again derived using the Ecu, when it delved as deep as 106.98 yen. \par \par \uc2  It subsequently rallied from that low to a peak of 164.07 yen in October last year, but has since come back a lot quicker. A 76.4 percent retracement of that rally gives a target at 120.45 and analysts see some psychological support at 120.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  However, with weekly charts showing a clear and strong downtrend, a retreat to 116.00 yen looked possible in the next few weeks, they said. \par \par \uc2  Immediate resistance would now be found around 122.60 and 123.20 yen and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to reclaim 124.45 resistance to put it on safer footing. \par \par \uc2  Analysts did emphasise that the bearish scenario assumed no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the BOJ and that there was a real chance the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step in to defend 122.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  They noted speculation in the market that a fall below this level would trigger panic selling by Japanese life insurers to hedge their massive euro debt exposure, losses from which could actually threaten the survivability of some institutions. \par \par \uc2  "Its always hard to know how much of their euro holdings are still unhedged, but it is thought to run into the many billions," said one analyst who declined to be named. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ will want to prevent a recurrence of financial instability at all costs, and if that means bailing these guys out by buying euro/yen, then so be it." ((Wayne Cole, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8584 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7j0489v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
