\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar falls to one-month lows below 120 yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 1999\par 11:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 19 (Reuters) - The dollar fell below 120 yen for the first time since June 18, the day the Bank of Japan bought euros for yen via the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had begun the week on a strong footing in Asia, hitting all-time highs against the euro, as traders tested Japan's commitment to preventing yen gains from derailing the country's nascent economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The yen extended gains against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Europe, gaining fresh energy from its advance against the dollar. The dollar fell as far as 119.97 yen by 0952 GMT while the euro plumbed new life lows of 121.67, down eight percent from its launch at the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  These euro/yen lows are equivalent to the mark's worst levels against the yen since August 1997. \par \par \uc2  Nervousness that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  was beginning to ebb ahead of Tuesday's Japanese public holiday. The yen's resilience in the wake of repeated rounds of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June was also encouraging dealers to drive the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher against the euro and the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "People are becoming less worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader at a U.S. bank in London. \par \par \uc2  ((Swaha Pattanaik, London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0