\par\par \b \uc2  MOF Mizoguchi -2: After Rumors Of BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Thu \b0\par\par\uc2 131 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1999\par 02:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Zembei Mizoguchi, international bureau head at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Friday declined to comment on whether the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Asked by reporters upon entering the ministry whether the BOJ had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar late Thursday, Mizoguchi said, "No comment." \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi said, however, he is "watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets carefully." \par \par \uc2  Late Thursday in Asian trade, the dollar rose nearly a yen to an intra-day high of Y121.17 after rumors circulated that the Bank of Japan had bought dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  At 0041 GMT Friday, the dollar was at Y120.87 and the euro was at Y123.35. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-07-99 \par \par \uc2  0043GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7g05aq9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
