\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dollar holds fire ahead of U.S. data. \b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1999\par 12:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 16 (Reuters) - The dollar hovered near 121 yen and $1.02 per euro by the European midsession on Friday, having held around those levels for the European morning. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said only U.S. data later on Friday were likely to pull the dollar out of pre-weekend lethargy, compounded by an upcoming holiday in Japan on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  June industrial production and capacity utilisation data are due at 1315 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "If we do not see a slowdown in growth coming through, the Fed will have to act further," said David Brickman, international economist at PaineWebber. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve raised its fed funds target rate to 5.0 percent on June 30. \par \par \uc2  The consensus in a quarterly Reuters poll published on Thursday was that the Fed will raise rates to 5.25 percent in the fourth quarter of 1999. \par \par \uc2  Industrial production is forecast to have risen 0.2 percent in June, while capacity utilisation is expected to be 80.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  The University of Michigan's July sentiment survey will also be released at 1400 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 120.81/86 yen at 1008 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to overnight highs of 121.12 yen amid concern over tensions between China and Taiwan. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's Sing Tao Daily reported mainland Chinese military movements had been detected in coastal areas facing Taiwan, and some civilian aviation had been disrupted on Thursday to allow military flights. \par \par \uc2  "The relationship with China has come into the equation from time to time, but it's not something that is going to have a serious impact on the dollar," said Brickman. \par \par \uc2  Fear of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also continued to keep the dollar above 120 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Economic Planning Agency chief Taichi Sakaiya said overnight the current dollar/yen rate around 120 yen was appropriate for Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan kept its zero interest rate policy after its monetary meeting, as expected. \par \par \uc2  The euro edged below $1.0189/93 from highs of $1.0211 and from $1.0216/21 in late Europe on Thursday, shrugging off another round of euro-supportive comments. \par \par \uc2  Incoming European monetary affairs commissioner Pedro Solbes said the success of the euro should not be judged only by its exchange rate, and that bond issuance showed it was a success. \par \par \uc2  Finnish Finance Minister Sauli Niinisto reiterated he saw potential for European growth and for a stronger euro. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the euro was digesting Thursday's comments from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg, who said the bank might gradually move towards a tightening stance on interest rates if monetary and credit expansion continued. \par \par \uc2  The euro failed to break through a strong barrier at $1.0260-70 on Thursday after the comments, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looked perky compared with Tuesday's life lows of $1.0104 and had scope to rise in the short term, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "We could move towards $1.03 but sentiment will remain very poor until there are clear signs of a turnaround in Euroland activity," said Keith Edmonds, chief analyst at IBJ. \par \par \uc2  "Parity remains the principal risk for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  German wholesale prices rose 0.2 percent in June month-on-month, below expectations. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7g04iu7\par }