\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr steady, supported by BOJ caution, Asia tension. \b0\par\par\uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1999\par 06:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 16 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady near 121 yen at midday in Tokyo on Friday, supported by expectations of possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) and by the growing threat of military tension in the Far East. \par \par \uc2  But its upside was capped by offers from Japanese exporters near 121.50 yen. The yen also found some support from continued strength in Tokyo share prices, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 120.88/93 yen at 0310 GMT, compared with 120.97/07 yen in New York late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0205/15, versus $1.0187/94 in late Thursday New York. \par \par \uc2  Late on Thursday in Tokyo, the dollar briefly rose as high as 121.40 yen from a low of 120.25 yen after the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the sixth in a recent series that started after Japan's gross domestic product data for the January-March quarter showed unexpectedly robust growth. \par \par \uc2  But unlike in the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japanese authorities refused to confirm Thursday's action. \par \par \uc2  "I have nothing in particular to say," Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said in a brief news conference on Friday when asked about the apparent yen-selling, dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Separately, Zembei Mizoguchi, head of the Finance Ministry's International Bureau, said on Friday he is watching movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market carefully. \par \par \uc2  Asked about news reports that the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, Mizuguchi said: "We should not comment whether we did or we did not." \par \par \uc2  "There seems to have been a shift in how \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is conducted," said a dealer at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  "After recent comments by (U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence) Summers, Japanese authorities might have decided it's wiser to keep a low profile when \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  Summers said last week that Tokyo should focus on economic fundamentals rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, and that manipulating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not lead to long-term prosperity. \par \par \uc2  In addition to BOJ caution, dealers were eager to square dollar/yen positions before the weekend amid growing tensions between China and Taiwan. \par \par \uc2  U.S. State Department Spokesman James Rubin on Thursday warned China that the United States would not tolerate a violent solution to the future of Taiwan. \par \par \uc2  Rubin spoke after China renewed its threat to retake Taiwan by force if it moved towards independence. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said another China factor capping the yen was speculation that Beijing might eventually decide to devalue the yuan. \par \par \uc2  Chinese Premier Zhu Rongji said the government will have to take further steps to boost the slowing economy, the official Financial News reported on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Zhu's comments seem to indicate that Chinese authorities are desperate to boost the economy," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  "Yuan devaluation speculation could heat up ahead of the 50th anniversary (of the founding of the People's Republic of China) in October," he added. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trapped in a range between $1.0188 and $1.0210 on Friday morning in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, the euro briefly rose as high as about $1.0252 after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) President Wim Duisenberg hinted at an eventual rise in interest rates for the 11-nation euro zone. \par \par \uc2  The euro was 123.33/38 yen at 0355 GMT, steady from around 123.33 yen in New York late on Thursday. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7g04i13\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
