\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dollar rises but lacks zip. \b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1999\par 10:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 16 (Reuters) - The dollar was firm against the yen and euro in Europe on Friday, but major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were within recent well-worn ranges, analysts and dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was broadly supported against the yen by the threat of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and also by signs of tension between China and Taiwan, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The market has focused on continued tensions between Taiwan and China, and is holding above 120 yen on fears that the Bank of Japan will come in," said Keith Edmonds, chief analyst at IBJ in London. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar rose overnight after a report in Hong Kong's Sing Tao Daily which said mainland Chinese military movements had been detected in coastal areas facing Taiwan, though Taiwan officials cast doubt on the report. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 120.84/89 yen at 0733 GMT, from overnight highs of 121.12 and from 120.48/58 in late European trade on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Wariness of the BOJ continued after Tokyo dealers detected Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying dollars for yen on Thursday. The dollar was also helped by short-covering ahead of a Japanese holiday on Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar failed to break above Thursday's high of 121.30 yen, as Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the lure of strong equity markets and signs of a nascent economic recovery, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials attempted overnight to put a brake on the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  Economic Planning Agency chief Taichi Sakaiya said the current dollar/yen rate around 120 yen was appropriate for Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami reiterated that the Japanese economy had stopped declining, but said there was no clear sign of recovery. \par \par \uc2  The euro hovered around $1.02 after failing to break key resistance at $1.0260-70 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Euro interest rate markets fell and the euro rose on Thursday after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg said the bank might gradually move towards a tightening stance on interest rates if monetary and credit expansion continued. \par \par \uc2  The euro backtracked to $1.0203/07 by 0805 GMT, from Thursday's high of $1.0252. \par \par \uc2  But it remains a cent above life lows of $1.0104 reached on Tuesday, and analysts said there was scope for further short-term upside. \par \par \uc2  "The euro could move higher if U.S. industrial production data are not very strong," said Giorgio Radaelli, head of research at First Chicago. \par \par \uc2  June industrial production, due at 1315 GMT, is forecast to rise 0.2 percent, while capacity utilisation is forecast at 80.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  "We could move towards $1.03 but sentiment will remain very poor until there are clear signs of a turnaround in Euroland activity," said Edmonds. \par \par \uc2  "Parity remains the principal risk for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  ((Carolyn Cohn, London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7g04hyc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
