\par\par \b \uc2  US refused MOF request to aid  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 -Nikkei. \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1999\par 14:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 16 (Reuters) - The U.S. last week refused a request from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun(Nikkei)newspaper said in its "Market Watcher" column on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The column quoted an unnamed international financial source as saying that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week apparently sounded out the New York Federal Reserve about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf. \par \par \uc2  The request was believed to have been made just before U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers' comment that Japan should focus on domestic demand rather than "manipulation" of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "However, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were said to have flatly refused," the newspaper said. \par \par \uc2  The column also quoted a U.S. embassy official in Tokyo as saying that at a time when Japan should be focusing on domestic demand, seeking to boost exports through a weaker yen was the wrong approach. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem the yen's rise amid concern in Tokyo that a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would choke off Japan's nascent economic recovery by making exports more expensive. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently stepped into the market for the sixth time in little more than a month as the yen approached 120 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo dealers said the BOJ had conducted its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  very secretively, and the action resulted in a just a shortlived dollar bounce above 121 yen. By Friday, the yen was drifting higher again, trading at around 120.70 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The earlier \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  had dragged the dollar back up from around 117 yen and hoisted it as high at 122.87 yen. The aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to have displeased other countries, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Asian governments do not want to see renewed downward pressure on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which could result from a sharply weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7g046jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
