\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr rangebound vs yen on caution over BOJ action. \b0\par\par\uc2 618 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1999\par 08:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 15 (Reuters) - The dollar moved narrowly against the yen in late afternoon Tokyo on Thursday in a market marking time amid expectations that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) could soon \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  Such expectations mounted as the dollar approached a psychologically important support point of 120 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 120.56/61 yen at 0612 GMT, after falling as low as 120.36 yen overnight in New York, its lowest level since June 18. \par \par \uc2  The euro was was $1.0225/28, compared with $1.0205/10 in New York late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said earlier on Thursday the ministry would consider an appropriate response to the dollar's recent fall against the yen, but the impact of his remarks on the market was limited. \par \par \uc2  "Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ineffective. There is also some doubt about the effectiveness of real \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as expectations have built up so much recently," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  five times in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since yen-buying pressures mounted after Japanese government data released last month showed a robust 1.9 percent growth in the nation's January-March gross domestic product (GDP). \par \par \uc2  The BOJ also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for the euro via the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) on June 18 and 21. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the dollar rose as high as 120.92 yen amid speculation that the BOJ might step in to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar reversed direction on selling by Japanese exporters and on a report quoting Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa as saying that 120 yen was not a level to worry about. \par \par \uc2  The dollar slipped as low as 120.42 yen before paring losses on comments by Miyazawa that the report was a "nuisance" and that there was no change in the policy of taking decisive action against any drastic rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2  "It's a nuisance," Miyazawa told Reuters when asked about the report. "I have no comment on this." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar was capped near 121 yen by offers from Japanese exporters and overseas fund operators. \par \par \uc2  "Overseas operators' yen bids may be linked to their investment in Japanese stocks. Such interest seems to be strong as the Nikkei continued to rise," said a dealer at a trust bank. Tokyo's benchmark Nikkei average ended up 74.00 points or 0.40 percent at 18,431.86 on Thursday, after earlier rising as high as 18,459.51, its highest intraday level since September 11, 1997. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market's attention could shift to next week's congressional testimony by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan if the U.S. consumer price index (CPI) for June, due at 1230 GMT on Thursday, fails to excite the market. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters forecast, on average, the CPI to show a rise of 0.1 percent overall and 0.2 percent excluding volatile energy and food prices. \par \par \uc2  The euro was slightly firmer ahead of a meeting on Thursday of the governing council of the ECB, as the market is cautious in case the council uses the regular post-meeting news conference to offer more than just verbal support for the euro. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were also reluctant to sell the euro actively against the yen due to possible euro-buying, yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at 123.15/28 yen as of 0648 GMT, compared with 123.15 yen in New York late on Wednesday. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7f04npi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
