\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CROSS-Euro easier vs yen, maintains BOJ vigil. \b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1999\par 05:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 15 (Reuters) - The euro was slightly lower against the yen by midday on Thursday, but was supported by the potential for yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro's gains against the yen were likely to be tempered, however, by persistent interest in selling euros for yen on rallies. "There are offers by Japanese exporters near 123.50 yen," a trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at 123.11/16 yen as of 0310 GMT, compared with 123.15 yen in late New York trade on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was reluctance to sell the euro actively, due to the possibility of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There has been wariness about possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (to buy euros for yen) since the euro fell to 122.64 yen (on Wednesday)," said a dealer for a European bank, noting that was close to the level where the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said large-lot buying of the euro for yen by a European bank on Wednesday fuelled rumours the BOJ may have conducted euro-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the euro was also supported by vague speculation about the potential for euro-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There are rumours flying around that there may be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or that the Bundesbank may be preparing to release some type of statement," said a dealer for another European bank. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at $1.0213/16 as of 0311 GMT, compared with $1.0205/10 in late New York. \par \par \uc2  But other dealers said the euro's firmness against the dollar was probably mainly a result of buy-backs by dealers seeking to lock in profits. \par \par \uc2  "I think market players who sold the euro earlier, thinking it would fall to parity against the dollar, are buying back," said the first dealer. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Wednesday that he hoped the euro's internal stability would one day be reflected in its external value. \par \par \uc2  But Tietmeyer declined to comment on the most recent decline in the euro and on whether recent economic data suggested that Europe's economic upturn was not gathering speed as hoped. \par \par \uc2  Speaking at a news conference to outline an internal restructirng of the Bundesbank, Tietmeyer said he would leave comments on those issues up to the ECB, whose governing council meets at 0700 GMT on Thursday and which will hold a news conference afterwards. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-5473-3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7f04nkg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
