\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Watching U.S. CPI, Taiwan. \b0\par\par\uc2 888 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1999\par 13:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 15 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were steady on Thursday as players waited for U.S. inflation figures and Asia kept a wary eye on the spat between Taiwan and China. \par \par \uc2  Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were slightly firmer but showed only muted reaction to apparent Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which briefly pushed dollar/yen to 121.30 before the greenback slipped back below 121. \par \par \uc2  The United States is due to announce June consumer price data at 1230 GMT, and global markets will watch closely for any sign of an inflationary threat that could lead to higher interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Figures released on Wednesday showed the U.S. producer price index (PPI) fell 0.1 percent in June, the first decline since February. \par \par \uc2  "If that (consumer price index) comes out benign just as the PPI did, then undoubtedly that's great news for emerging markets round the world," said Callum Henderson, emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank in London. \par \par \uc2  "But that's a big if, and we'll wait on tenterhooks for that number." \par \par \uc2  Tension between Taiwan and China continued to unnerve East Asian markets after Taipei said at the weekend it was dropping the "one China" policy that has helped maintain security in the region. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar rebounded from an early plunge against the U.S. dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called a hasty news conference to reaffirm its pledge to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market where necessary. \par \par \uc2  London-based analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at least once earlier in the week to limit the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's downside. \par \par \uc2  But Taiwan non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) had come under substantial pressure, they said, shifting from a discount to a premium against spot rates. One-year NDFs were quoted at a premium of 0.22 bid over spot in the London morning. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong dollar and Chinese yuan forwards had also come under pressure, the analysts added, although U.S./Hong Kong dollar forwards closed slightly softer on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general were still in a slightly jittery mood after the Latin America turmoil that took hold at the start of the week, although worries that Argentina might not honour its debts had now faded. \par \par \uc2  Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were unmoved in London morning trade. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty, which slipped to just over five percent above its basket parity on Tuesday, continued its recovery to reach 5.76 percent above the midpoint by mid-morning. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the zloty is likely to march on towards nine or 10 percent in the next few months, lifted by strong Polish fundamentals and surging inflows of foreign direct investment. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown slid in nervous early trade ahead of a regular \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board meeting, after signals from board members on Wednesday that it was considering action against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent strength. \par \par \uc2  But it rebounded after a brief \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement that the board would not take any monetary decisions on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to be trying to talk down the crown, but threats of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be taken seriously. \par \par \uc2  The South African rand continued to suffer from languishing gold prices, weakening despite falling repo rates and the recovery in emerging market sentiment as the precious metal plumbed fresh 20-year lows below $254 a troy ounce. ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, including the change versus late New York trade the previous day and the change in the year to date.. ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted against the dollar. ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab     36.71   36.75   -0.11%   5.50%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab    3.98    3.99   -0.23%  -2.19%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 249.27  249.14    0.05%  -0.76%\par Slovakia\tab \tab \tab 44.87   44.90   -0.07%   4.35%\par Romania\tab \tab \tab 15,920  15,870    0.32%  45.39%\par Ukraine\tab \tab \tab   3.96    3.96   -0.03%   0.69%\par South Africa\tab \tab    6.15    6.12    0.46%   5.21%\par Kenya\tab \tab \tab    72.23   72.15    0.11%  17.26%\par Israel\tab \tab \tab   4.080   4.084   -0.10%  -0.94%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LATAM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexico\t