\par\par \b \uc2  Japan tactics wearing thin with trade partners. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kanta Watanabe \par \uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1999\par 16:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Reuters) - Selling the yen may be a painless way of boosting Japan's economy, but Tokyo's tactics will be increasingly difficult to sell to the nation's trade partners, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars six times in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since the market's appetite for the yen was whetted in June by news of unexpectedly strong economic growth in the first three months of this year. \par \par \uc2  The latest move came on Thursday, when it was seen briefly buying dollars after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit 120.25 yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for the euro via the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 18 and 21. \par \par \uc2  While there were few grumbles from abroad after the first round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June, more recent yen-selling moves by BOJ have been at higher dollar levels and have raised suspicions that Japan is using the yen as a trade tool. \par \par \uc2  "There was no problem with the June 10 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that came on the GDP (gross domestic product) announcement day," said Takehiro Sato, assistant manager of the treasury group at Sumitomo Bank. \par \par \uc2  That was because the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came as the dollar fell near a level, which if reached could have forced Japanese exporters to cut their earnings forecasts, Sato said. \par \par \uc2  "But \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on subsequent dates would not have won approval from other G7 (Group of Seven) nations or Asian countries," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 10 came as the dollar dipped as low as 117.63 yen after the release of the GDP data, which showed stunning 1.9 percent growth in January-March GDP. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's quarterly "tankan" corporate survey released earlier this month showed that major manufacturers assumed a dollar/yen exchange rate of 116.78 yen in their business plans for the fiscal year to next March 31. \par \par \uc2  But the BOJ's July 5 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started from levels below 121.50 yen and continued above 122 yen, pushing the greenback as high as 122.87 yen that day. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese firms may be basing their business plans on a dollar/yen exchange rate of around 116 yen, but a survey by the Economic Planning Agency (EPA) showed that their break-even point is actually much lower," Sumitomo's Sato said. \par \par \uc2  A survey of 1,361 firms released in April by the EPA showed that the average break-even level was 112.70 yen to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Japan's tactics drew perhaps their most explicit show of displeasure last week, when new U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said Tokyo should focus on economic fundamentals rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. "Manipulating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not the approach that leads to long-term prosperity," Summers said in a television interview. \par \par \uc2  Ryutaro Kono, senior economist at Dai-Ichi Life Research Institute, said: "I think Summers' message was that yen weakness accompanied by fiscal expansion and low interest rates is acceptable, but just using a weak yen as a tool is not." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Japanese officials appear to be toning down their enthusiasm for a weak yen in response to such criticism. \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda, Japan's new vice finance minister for international affairs, told Reuters Wednesday that Japan was not seeking specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. \par \par \uc2  Asked his view on the possible impact on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and economies of yen weakness resulting from \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Kuroda said: "We don't intend to orchestrate a weaker yen." \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said cooperation among (G7) nations on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained solid, but analysts see any concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as unlikely at current dollar/yen levels. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is already quite strong against the euro. So the United States is unlikely to wish its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen further against the yen," Dai-Ichi's Kono said. \par \par \uc2  Sumitomo's Sato said: "Concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unthinkable unless, say, the dollar dips below 110 yen towards 105 yen." \par \par \uc2  It is also risky to assume that the United States' strong dollar policy - pursued vigorously by Summers' predecessor Robert Rubin - will continue forever, Kono added. \par \par \uc2  "The saying that 'a strong dollar is in the interest of the United States' only applies when the U.S. economy is doing well. So there may be a shift in the Treasury's dollar policy when the economy slows down," he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 120.53/63 yen in late Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7f04h03\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
