\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-BOJ lifts dollar from its 4-week low vs yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 643 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1999\par 11:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 15 (Reuters) - The dollar rose from a four-week low against the yen in late Tokyo trade on Thursday, springing up when the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's bounce was limited as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move had been widely anticipated, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 120.90/95 yen at 0759 GMT after jumping as high as 121.40 yen on the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a low of 120.25 yen, its lowest level since June 18, they said. \par \par \uc2  Market sources said the BOJ's dollar buying was conducted in a secretive manner through a limited number of commercial banks in Tokyo and possibly in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar jumped more than one yen after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it quickly lost about half a yen from its high," said a dealer at a Japanese bank. "A lot of people had been waiting for the BOJ to step in. The market's appetite for yen is very strong." \par \par \uc2  Thursday's BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the sixth in a recent series that started after Japan's gross domestic product (GDP) data for the first three months of this year showed unexpectedly robust quarter-on-quarter growth of 1.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on July 5, when it began buying dollars below 121.50 yen and during the course of the day pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as high as 122.87 yen. \par \par \uc2  Ryohei Muramatsu, manager of treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Commerzbank in Tokyo, said: "The time for yen buying is ripe. The market's direction won't change despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  "Although the dollar may not immediately break below 120 yen, I think we could see another yen-buying move in an hour or two, after the market regains calm," he added. \par \par \uc2  This was because foreign investors' appetite for Japanese stocks remained strong, Muramatsu said. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's key Nikkei average ended up 74.00 points or 0.40 percent at 18,431.86 on Thursday, after earlier rising as high as 18,459.51, its highest intraday level since September 11, 1997. \par \par \uc2  Early on Thursday morning, the dollar dropped on a report quoting Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa as saying that 120 yen was not a level to worry about. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback pared losses by late morning after Miyazawa called the report a "nuisance" and said there was no change in Japan's policy of taking decisive action against any drastic rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2  "It's a nuisance," Miyazawa told Reuters when asked about the report. "I have no comment on this." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some Japanese exporters and overseas fund operators were still keen to sell dollars above 121 yen. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister Nobuaki Usui said late on Thursday that Japan will watch movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets more closely than before and will take appropriate action if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the Japanese monetary authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market or took action in late Thursday trade, Usui told reporters he could not comment on daily market movements and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Rapid strengthening of the yen is undesirable not only for the Japanese economy but also for the global economy. It is important that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  move in a stable manner," Usui said. \par \par \uc2  The euro also gained against the yen in late trade in line with the rise in the dollar/yen rate. \par \par \uc2  Judging from a lack of significant movement in the euro/dollar rate, there was probably no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros for yen by the BOJ, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at 123.30/40 yen as of 0850 GMT, compared with 123.15 yen in New York late on Wednesday. ((Kanta Watanabe, Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv7f04g0z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
