\par\par \b \uc2  Sakakibara: Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Indispensable-Nikkei \b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1999\par 21:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Nikkei)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's influential former vice finance minister for international affairs, Eisuke Sakakibara, said in an interview Wednesday that government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is an indispensable tool in an imperfect market, The Nihon Keizai Shimbun Thursday morning edition reported. \par \par \uc2  "Prices are ultimately set by the market, but the market is not perfect," Sakakibara told the newspaper in an interview. \par \par \uc2  "The government has a role - not opposing the market, but complementing it," he said, noting that "\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are one way of doing this." \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara retired from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  on July 8. His successor, Haruhiko Kuroda, has already made it clear that he will continue Sakakibara's basic policy stance. \par \par \uc2  "With globalization and the spread of the virtual economy," Sakakibara said, "the market will inevitably overreact at times, so smoothing out \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations is necessary." \par \par \uc2  "When an overreaction occurs, it's vital to hold a dialogue with the markets and correct it," he said. "Leaving everything to the markets will cripple capitalism." \par \par \uc2  According to Sakakibara, Japan's recent economic situation is reminiscent of 1993 and 1994. At that time, capital spending was rebounding and stocks climbing, but a sharp upturn in the yen set back economic recovery by at least one year. Based on that experience, he said, the ministry has been conducting "preventive" \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I don't mean to suggest that exports should be expanded through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but can the economy recover smoothly if the dollar suddenly hits Y115 or Y110?" he asked. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-07-99 \par \par \uc2  1906GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv7e05apv\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 17/10/1999\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\b